{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And he shall be brought to the priest.</b> Scripture says that this is the law of the metzora on the day he wishes to become purified — that he shall be brought to the priest, for he has no purification ever except by his word. After that it explains that the priest goes out to the place of his dwelling outside the camp, and he does not come to him even though he has healed. And its midrash in Torat Kohanim (parashah 1:3): \"And he shall be brought to the priest\" — he shall not delay. If so, Scripture says that on the day he becomes purified, when he heals from his affliction, he is brought against his will to the priest. And similarly, \"And when the zav is cleansed of his discharge\" (Leviticus 15:13), \"And if she is cleansed of her discharge\" (Leviticus 15:28) — when they cease and become clean of it, as I explained (Ramban on Leviticus 15:11), and this is correct:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:53:39.703874030Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}